al buying a brand-new wardrobe  is super expensive and as previously  mentioned the vast majority of the  bachelor contestants are never paid for  appearing on the reality dating show so  applying to the show is a huge gamble  many of these women have to quit their  jobs buy new wardrobes and continue  paying their mortgages while starring on  the ABC series  knowing this contestants are all the  more driven to win the bachelors  but to do this they have to stand out  which makes buying an impressive  wardrobe that much more important  former contestant Jillian Harris had to  remortgage her house before appearing on  the show and she's spent a whopping  eight thousand dollars on new clothes  but that amount pales in comparison to  how much a season 20 contestants spent  on her new wardrobe  Olivia Caridi is rumored to have spent  around forty thousand dollars on clothes  all while respecting the - suitcase /  contestant rule cut all contact with the  outside world now this rule may seem  like a given but that doesn't make it  any easier to follow most people aren't  glued to their phones and are accustomed  to using the internet at leisure but  when you become a contestant on The  Bachelor you have to kiss technology  goodbye contestants have to disconnect  from the outside world they can't call  their mom's to vent about their feelings  or talk about the Mean Girls on the show  and they can't catch up with their best  friends they're completely alienated  from the outside world watching TV or  staying up to date with current events  just isn't allowed and not knowing  what's going on around you can make  keeping your head in the game all the  more challenging but ABC executives just  can't risk letting their contestants  spoil their season's events before it  hits the small screen but at least the  contestants have a beautiful mansion to  explore right well not exactly  did you know that the mansion doesn't  have any AC that's right  air conditioning makes too much